Derive the following Two-Level Systems and the Schottky Anomaly relation from the preceding result, showing the algebra, calculus, counting, or physical identity used at each step.
\[
C_{V,1}=\frac{du}{dT}
=\frac{du}{dx}\frac{dx}{dT}
=\left(-\frac{\Delta e^x}{(1+e^x)^2}\right)\left(-\frac{x}{T}\right)
=k_{\mathrm B}x^2\frac{e^x}{(1+e^x)^2}
=k_{\mathrm B}\left(\frac{x}{2}\right)^2\operatorname{sech}^2\left(\frac{x}{2}\right).
\tag*{[3]}
\]
